From: HomeKMS maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] Keep RPC associations open between activation requests

The upstream handler explicitly closes after one activation response, although
its bind acknowledgement advertises multiplexing. Clients which retain the RPC
association fail, or reconnect with a warning (vlmcs). Continue the existing
receive loop until EOF/error instead, and use sendall to avoid a short response.
No bind or KMS payload semantics are changed.

--- a/py-kms/pykms_Server.py
+++ b/py-kms/pykms_Server.py
@@ -521,9 +521,9 @@
                                 pretty_printer(num_text = [-3, 18, 19], where = "srv")

                         try:
-                                self.request.send(res)
-                                if packetType == rpcBase.packetType['request']:
-                                        break
+                                # One RPC association may carry multiple requests.
+                                # Only EOF or a transport error ends the connection.
+                                self.request.sendall(res)
                         except socket.error as e:
                                 pretty_printer(log_obj = loggersrv.error,
                                                put_text = "{reverse}{red}{bold}While sending: %s{end}" %str(e))
